
******* Unpublished Flexible Water Models ***************

The quadratic stretching and bending
terms are evaluated as in JACS 118, 112255 (1996). Units for force constants
are kcal/mol-A^2 and kcal/mol-rad^2. I used Pettitt's force constants for
TIP3F and my own for TIP4F. Both models give good properties for liquid water
at 25C and 1 atm; neither gives a T of max density near 4 C at 1 atm. The
heat capacities are, of course, too high. Bill

